Pyrite64's engine (n64/engine at ec98ba1) built with our toolchain (GCC 16.2, libdragon 39d0d60).

The engine builds with -Wall -Wextra -Werror. GCC 16 warns about tiny3d's own designated
initializers in C++ (t3d_viewport_create in t3d.h: -Wmissing-field-initializers), and the engine's
headers have unused parameters that -Wextra reports, so the build stops on code that isn't wrong.
This keeps the warnings and stops treating them as errors.

tools/n64-pyrite64.sh applies it to a copy of n64/engine in build/n64/p64-work, which the editor
copies into the project; the Pyrite64 checkout stays as fetched.

